<InfoPage path="/responsible-gaming/" label="Responsible gaming" heading="Responsible Gaming: Set Limits Before You Start" title="Yarrwin Responsible Gaming Guide | Safer Play Habits" description="Practical responsible-gaming habits for adults, including spending limits, breaks and avoiding loss chasing.">
  <h2>Set a firm budget</h2><p>Only use money you can afford to lose, and decide the amount before opening a game. Never borrow, use bill money or increase a stake to recover a loss.</p>
  <h2>Control time and attention</h2><p>Set a session timer, take breaks and stop when the timer ends. If the platform supports deposit limits, cool-off periods or self-exclusion, check the current account settings and use them when needed.</p>
  <h2>Know when to pause</h2><p>If play affects sleep, work, relationships or your mood, stop and speak with someone you trust. Gaming is for adults aged 18+ where permitted by local rules.</p>
</InfoPage>
